        {
          "url": "https://github.com/ovelhaaa/hydra-tape-engine/pull/59#discussion_r4660702896",
          "path": "scripts/generate_phase73_web_listening.mjs",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Enable multiple heads in the multi-head listening scenario**\n\nWhen generating the Phase 7.3 A/C listening package, this scenario enables only the third playback head: `activeHeads` is passed unchanged through the worklet/C API and interpreted as a bitmask in `TapeCore::Impl::updateCachedParams()`, so `4` selects only bit 2. Consequently, the WAVs labeled “Multi-Head + Ping-Pong” do not exercise the head interactions that this scenario is intended to evaluate. Use a mask with multiple bits set (such as `7`) and regenerate the comparison evidence.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->"
        },
